      "content": "I would advise you to consult a pediatrician as soon as possible. The symptoms you described, such as a fever and small, red/purplish spots, can be a sign of several things, including heat rash, eczema, or a viral infection. Although the spots didn't change color with the glass test, this doesn't necessarily mean it's heat rash either, and only a professional can determine the cause. In the meantime, keep a close eye on your child's temperature and watch for any other concerning symptoms.",
